ROOT CAUSE OF THIN-WALL WARP IS NOW DERIVED.

Do not change D, TXC, WXF, wall projection, or DDA stepping.

The hEdges/vEdges packing is correct.

The bug is that the edge lookup uses the ENTERED cell without compensating for
the DDA step direction.

==================================================
EDGE STORAGE CONVENTION
==================================================

The editor/source defines:

    hEdges[row][col]
        = SOUTH edge of cell row,col
        = boundary between row and row+1

    vEdges[row][col]
        = EAST edge of cell row,col
        = boundary between col and col+1

Packing:

    H: 13 rows x 14 cols
       index = row*14 + col

    V: 14 rows x 13 cols
       index = row*13 + col

That part is correct and must not be changed.

==================================================
WHAT DDA MX/MY MEAN
==================================================

The DDA does:

    MX = MX + SIX
or
    MY = MY + SIY

BEFORE performing the edge lookup.

Therefore MX/MY represent the cell the ray has JUST ENTERED.

But the physical boundary just crossed is not always stored against that cell.

It depends on step sign.

==================================================
SID=0 — VERTICAL BOUNDARY / vEdges
==================================================

SID=0 means MX changed.

Current:

    EI=MY*13+MX+1

Interpretation:
    vEdges[MY][MX]

This is correct only for SIX=-1.

CASE SIX=-1:

    old cell: col MX+1
    new cell: col MX

The ray crossed the WEST boundary of the old cell.

That is the EAST edge of the NEW cell:

    vEdges[MY][MX]

So current lookup is correct.

CASE SIX=+1:

    old cell: col MX-1
    new cell: col MX

The ray crossed the EAST edge of the OLD cell:

    vEdges[MY][MX-1]

Current lookup instead asks for:

    vEdges[MY][MX]

which is one boundary too far right.

==================================================
SID=1 — HORIZONTAL BOUNDARY / hEdges
==================================================

SID=1 means MY changed.

Current:

    EI=MY*14+MX+1

Interpretation:
    hEdges[MY][MX]

This is correct only for SIY=-1.

CASE SIY=-1:

    old row: MY+1
    new row: MY

The ray crossed the NORTH boundary of the old cell.

That is the SOUTH edge of the NEW cell:

    hEdges[MY][MX]

Current lookup is correct.

CASE SIY=+1:

    old row: MY-1
    new row: MY

The ray crossed the SOUTH edge of the OLD cell:

    hEdges[MY-1][MX]

Current lookup instead asks for:

    hEdges[MY][MX]

which is one boundary too far down.

==================================================
MINIMAL FIX
==================================================

Preserve the existing 1-based string indexing.

A minimally invasive form is:

    EI=0

    IF WV=0 AND SID=1 THEN EI=MY*14+MX+1
    IF WV=0 AND SID=1 AND SIY=1 THEN EI=EI-14

    IF WV=0 AND SID=0 THEN EI=MY*13+MX+1
    IF WV=0 AND SID=0 AND SIX=1 THEN EI=EI-1

Then existing:

    IF EI<1 THEN EI=1
    IF EI>182 THEN EI=1
    IF WV=0 AND SID=1 AND HW$(EI:EI)="1" THEN WV=8
    IF WV=0 AND SID=0 AND VW$(EI:EI)="1" THEN WV=8

can remain.

This gives:

VERTICAL:
    SIX=-1 -> MY*13+MX+1
    SIX=+1 -> MY*13+MX

HORIZONTAL:
    SIY=-1 -> MY*14+MX+1
    SIY=+1 -> (MY-1)*14+MX+1

which exactly matches the editor's east/south ownership convention.

==================================================
DO NOT "FIX" THE STRIDES
==================================================

Do not change:

    horizontal stride 14
    vertical stride 13

They are correct.

The handoff already disproved the stride theory:

    HW = 13*14 = 182
    VW = 14*13 = 182

Reader and writer agree.

==================================================
DO NOT CHANGE DISTANCE
==================================================

Once the correct edge is identified, the existing wall distance is already the
distance to the boundary just crossed:

    SID=0:
        D=SDX-DDX

    SID=1:
        D=SDY-DDY

That is exactly where an edge wall physically lives.

Do NOT add:

    half-cell offsets
    +/- DDX
    +/- DDY

to compensate for the lookup error.

That would turn an indexing bug into a geometry bug.

==================================================
DO NOT CHANGE TXC
==================================================

Likewise, after the correct edge becomes WV=8:

    IF SID=0 THEN WXF=PY+D*RY
    ELSE WXF=PX+D*RX

is the normal coordinate along the boundary.

Do not change WXF/TXC unless the wall remains texture-warped AFTER the lookup
fix.

First fix which physical edge is being hit.

